    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0430" n="1244" xml:id="pg1244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Eisenhower papers, Whitman
                    file</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum for the President, Prepared in the United
                        States Atomic Energy Commission</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d119-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-11-10">November 10, 1953</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The atomic energy relationships between the United States and Canada, if they
                    come up during your visit,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d119-f2"/> should be currently
                    benefited as we will be informing the Canadians today of the arrangement for
                    more extensive technical cooperation under the <hi rendition="#italic">Modus
                        Vivendi.</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d119-f3"/> This will give them
                    information on effects of atomic weapons to assist them in defense
                    preparations.</p>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Suggested points that might be made if
                        occasion arises:</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Express appreciation of the American people for the Canadian contribution
                        to the common defense effort by the production and sale of uranium to the
                        United States—stressing particularly the sympathetic and understanding
                        cooperation of C.D. Howe.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Express hope that continued vigorous search for uranium will result in
                        greater production.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>State that you have directed the Chairman of the Atomic Energy Commission
                        to recommend amendments to the Atomic Energy Act at next session of Congress
                        to provide for broader cooperation with Canada and friendly nations.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d119-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d119-f1-content">
                <p>The source text is unsigned but was prepared on AEC stationery. It was initialed
                    “D.E.” by President Eisenhower.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d119-f2" n="2" xml:id="d119-f2-content">
                <p>The President visited Canada Nov. 13–14. No record of discussions on atomic
                    energy has been found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d119-f3" n="3" xml:id="d119-f3-content">
                <p>They <hi rendition="#italic">Modus Vivendi</hi> is recorded in the minutes of the
                    Combined Policy Committee, Jan. 7, 1948; for text, see <ref
                        target="frus1948v01p2#pg_679"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                        Relations</hi>, 1948, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, Part 2, p.
                        679</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
